<p>Now, how to design your controller endpoint points is more nuanced. If your application does not use libraries to group contextual business logic processes, then perhaps a series of condition statements in your controller method will suffice. Just try not to build &quot;fat controllers&quot;. If you find too much logic is being implemented in a controller method, you might try to split it up into private controller methods called by the public controller method.</p>
<p>I don't exactly know how you'll handle the different responses, but generally you should echo a json encoded string back to the AJAX call.</p>
